---
// src/components/PlayerEval/EvalAbout.astro
// Long-form context for the evaluation. Sits below the form so the form stays
// immediately reachable from the hero.
---

<section class="about">
  <div class="about-inner">
    <div class="about-head">
      <span class="eyebrow-sm">About the Session</span>
      <h2 class="about-title">What a Player Evaluation Actually Involves</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="about-cols">
      <div class="about-col">
        <h3 class="about-sub">On the day</h3>
        <p>
          A South Van FC evaluation is a training session, not a queue and a
          clipboard. Players warm up, work through technical work with the ball,
          and then play. Most of what we learn comes from the small-sided games
          at the end, because that is where decisions get made under real
          pressure. If you have been searching for soccer tryouts in Vancouver,
          this is our version of one: the same look at your ability, without
          cutting anyone at the end of it.
        </p>
        <p>
          Sessions run in South Vancouver and are led by our <a
            href="/our-coaches/">coaching staff</a
          >, not an assistant with a checklist. Bring boots, shin pads, and a
          ball if you have one. Players under 18 need a parent or guardian to
          confirm consent on the form above.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="about-col">
        <h3 class="about-sub">What you get back</h3>
        <p>
          Every player is scored 1 to 5 across the four pillars: technical,
          tactical, physical, and mental. You receive that as a written report,
          along with the two or three things we would work on first and an
          honest view of where the player currently sits. The scores are
          development tools. They are not used to rank players against each
          other or to gatekeep entry.
        </p>
        <p>
          There is no obligation after the session. If the fit is right, the
          report becomes the starting point for an individual development plan
          inside the <a href="/soccer-academy/">academy programme</a>, and you
          can review <a href="/soccer-academy/pricing/">programme pricing</a> at
          your own pace. If it is not the right fit, you keep the feedback
          anyway.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="about-foot">
      Curious what coaches are actually watching for before you book? Our guide
      to <a href="/blogs/what-coaches-look-for-at-tryouts/"
        >what coaches look for at tryouts</a
      > breaks it down.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .about {
    background: #fff;
    padding: 64px 80px;
    border-top: 1px solid #eef0f7;
  }
  .about-inner {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 32px;
  }
  .about-head {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 8px;
  }
  .eyebrow-sm {
    font-size: 10px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 3px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #e8b430;
  }
  .about-title {
    font-family: "Inter Variable", sans-serif;
    font-size: clamp(24px, 2.6vw, 34px);
    letter-spacing: 0.5px;
    color: #011f4a;
    line-height: 1.2;
  }

  .about-cols {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 48px;
  }
  .about-col {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 14px;
  }
  .about-sub {
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.3px;
    color: #013478;
    padding-bottom: 10px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #eef0f7;
  }
  .about-col p,
  .about-foot {
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: #3d4d6e;
  }
  .about-foot {
    padding-top: 24px;
    border-top: 1px solid #eef0f7;
    font-size: 13px;
    color: #6b7a9e;
  }

  .about a {
    color: #013478;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
    text-decoration-color: rgba(1, 52, 120, 0.3);
    transition: text-decoration-color 0.2s;
  }
  .about a:hover {
    text-decoration-color: #013478;
  }

  @media (max-width: 960px) {
    .about {
      padding: 48px 28px;
    }
    .about-cols {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 32px;
    }
  }
</style>
